A rendered Nano's reply follows the route window through one rule applied by the transport finalizer. The retired
"bounded output target" phrase hid that the send re-measured the request on an uncalibrated basis and could cut the
reply to tens of tokens (the Codex Cowork incident) or send the whole ceiling over a 128K window. The paragraph now
names the rule and where it runs, the stand-in for an unknown window, the exact local shortfall and its one recovery,
the Max-only task-local Low and the forced final's shared measurement, so the chapter stays the map of the mechanism.
